1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:06,500
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

2
00:00:06,633 --> 00:00:10,667
[SIKLAB SINGING "UNFORGETTABLE"]

3
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,267
<i> Sometimes I think of you.</i>

4
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,333
<i> The kid is completely drained.</i>

5
00:00:16,467 --> 00:00:19,333
<i>They've been doing nonstop
local tours with Siklab.</i>

6
00:00:20,333 --> 00:00:23,000
<i>I'll still find my way back
to you</i>

7
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:26,933
[TENSE MUSIC]

8
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:29,133
<i>- Miguel!
- Miguel.</i>

9
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:38,367
<i>I know who was behind
the destruction of our resort.</i>

10
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,600
<i> It's my dear sister Serina.</i>

11
00:00:40,733 --> 00:00:42,700
<i> So, it's you.</i>

12
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:45,767
<i> Angel of Gran Vista Resort.</i>

13
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:49,733
<i>I'm Serina of
the Montaverde Group of Hotels.</i>

14
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:51,700
<i>I want your resort
to go bankrupt</i>

15
00:00:51,833 --> 00:00:54,333
<i>so I can buy it
for the Montaverde Empire.</i>

16
00:00:54,467 --> 00:00:56,700
<i>Mama Bebe, Grandfather Xavi,
and I already know</i>

17
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,467
<i>that you were the one
who told those boys</i>

18
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,333
<i> to sabotage our resort.</i>

19
00:01:00,467 --> 00:01:01,633
<i> How dare you?</i>

20
00:01:04,267 --> 00:01:06,600
<i>Why are you picking a fight
with a child?</i>

21
00:01:07,033 --> 00:01:08,633
<i> Why are you taking her side?</i>

22
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:10,033
<i>You don't even know
what happened.</i>

23
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:12,600
<i>Why are you being so nice
to that random teenage girl?</i>

24
00:01:12,733 --> 00:01:15,033
<i>Why? Do you miss your daughter
that much?</i>

25
00:01:15,167 --> 00:01:16,167
<i> Young lady.</i>

26
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:19,633
<i> Are you okay?</i>

27
00:01:19,767 --> 00:01:20,967
<i> Like every other kid,</i>

28
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:24,400
<i>you see your dead daughter
in that Angel.</i>

29
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:25,600
<i> I will never stop</i>

30
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:28,333
<i>until their pathetic
little resort goes bankrupt.</i>

31
00:01:28,467 --> 00:01:29,967
<i> And you can't stop me.</i>

32
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:32,567
<i>- Serina, where are you going?
- What?</i>

33
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:35,000
<i> Sir, you need to see this.</i>

34
00:01:35,133 --> 00:01:38,133
<i>Serina, how could you betray me?</i>

35
00:01:40,033 --> 00:01:41,600
<i> We've all played already.</i>

36
00:01:41,767 --> 00:01:43,100
<i> Your turn now.</i>

37
00:01:43,233 --> 00:01:45,600
<i>- And why would I?
- Unless you're intimidated...</i>

38
00:01:45,733 --> 00:01:47,667
<i>by this little lie-detector
gadget.</i>

39
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,500
<i> That's nothing but a toy.</i>

40
00:01:49,633 --> 00:01:50,567
<i> What's the question?</i>

41
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,833
<i>So, Calix, do you have feelings
for Angel?</i>

42
00:01:52,967 --> 00:01:57,467
[INTENSE MUSIC]

43
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:01,767
["YOU'RE MY FAVORITE SONG"
BY PRINCESS ALIYAH]

44
00:02:34,433 --> 00:02:36,433
What kind of stupid question
is that, Charm?

45
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:39,267
Of course I don't have feelings
for Angel.

46
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:51,300
That means you're lying.

47
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:54,000
So, you like Angel?

48
00:02:55,833 --> 00:02:57,433
Of course not. You know what?

49
00:02:57,567 --> 00:02:59,367
I don't want to play this...

50
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:01,300
I'm not playing
this stupid game anymore!

51
00:03:01,433 --> 00:03:03,333
I don't like Angel.
I could never like her.

52
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:10,067
[TENSE MUSIC]

53
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:12,333
What kind of question was that,
Charm?

54
00:03:12,467 --> 00:03:13,633
You really got him worked up.

55
00:03:13,767 --> 00:03:16,200
He might not let us copy answers
during the exam later.

56
00:03:16,333 --> 00:03:17,200
Let's go.

57
00:03:17,333 --> 00:03:18,533
Let's go home.

58
00:03:21,767 --> 00:03:23,000
Boys, wait for me.

59
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,800
So, it's confirmed.

60
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,833
Calix likes Angel.

61
00:03:29,967 --> 00:03:32,700
[FOREBODING MUSIC]

62
00:03:32,833 --> 00:03:34,633
I have a plan, Adie.

63
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:39,133
I'll make sure Calix
hates Angel forever...

64
00:03:39,267 --> 00:03:40,233
after this.

65
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,767
And what's the plan?

66
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,733
Let's put your hacking skills
to the test.

67
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:50,000
Time to go, cyber ninja.

68
00:04:06,267 --> 00:04:08,433
Honey, come on.
Give me a ride home.

69
00:04:10,133 --> 00:04:12,633
To the husband who's always
fighting with you?

70
00:04:12,767 --> 00:04:15,167
I'm not about to et her win,
am I?

71
00:04:18,933 --> 00:04:20,500
Why don't you come
with me instead?

72
00:04:28,233 --> 00:04:29,500
Are you serious?

73
00:04:34,133 --> 00:04:37,167
I make a lot of money
at that casino where we met.

74
00:04:37,300 --> 00:04:38,900
I have a lot of connections
there...

75
00:04:39,033 --> 00:04:40,400
influential people...

76
00:04:40,533 --> 00:04:43,100
even some truly ruthless ones.

77
00:04:43,233 --> 00:04:46,067
But I gave all of that up
for you, Serina.

78
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:48,033
I agreed to be your driver...

79
00:04:48,167 --> 00:04:49,233
because I love you.

80
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:51,633
Oh, Tyrone.

81
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:53,833
You know...

82
00:04:53,967 --> 00:04:55,800
if things were that simple...

83
00:04:55,933 --> 00:04:56,900
I'd go with you.

84
00:04:58,733 --> 00:05:00,500
But for now...

85
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:02,467
this is all I can give you.

86
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:12,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

87
00:05:14,567 --> 00:05:16,433
You probably thought I wouldn't
be able to track you down?

88
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:20,000
Enrico?

89
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:23,667
Enrico...

90
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:24,867
- it's not what you think.
- Enough. Enough!

91
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,633
You've been deceiving me
for so long.

92
00:05:31,267 --> 00:05:32,300
No. That's not true.

93
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:33,433
What do you mean it's not?

94
00:05:34,467 --> 00:05:35,533
There you go.

95
00:05:35,667 --> 00:05:36,767
That's what you're good at...

96
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:38,700
gaslighting people.

97
00:05:38,833 --> 00:05:41,533
Twisting all of your mistakes
around...

98
00:05:41,667 --> 00:05:43,533
and making me feel like
I'm the one who's wrong.

99
00:05:45,267 --> 00:05:46,600
What are you talking about?

100
00:05:46,733 --> 00:05:47,700
There.

101
00:05:49,233 --> 00:05:50,667
That bracelet he's wearing.

102
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,200
Right?

103
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:55,900
I suspected something about it,
but you told me it was nothing.

104
00:05:56,033 --> 00:05:58,033
You got so defensive,
didn't you?

105
00:05:58,167 --> 00:05:59,567
<i>That bracelet Tyrone
is wearing...</i>

106
00:06:01,267 --> 00:06:02,733
<i>you gave it to him, didn't you?</i>

107
00:06:02,867 --> 00:06:04,133
<i> You bought it from Roxanne?</i>

108
00:06:06,133 --> 00:06:08,133
<i>He just asked me to buy it
for him.</i>

109
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:10,400
<i>Tyrone has a girlfriend
in the U.S.,</i>

110
00:06:10,533 --> 00:06:12,333
<i> an old hag who gives him money</i>

111
00:06:12,467 --> 00:06:14,033
<i> whom he met at a casino.</i>

112
00:06:14,167 --> 00:06:16,167
<i> Despite everything that I did,</i>

113
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:20,233
<i>you have the nerve to accuse me
of having an affair?</i>

114
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:23,700
But it turns out...

115
00:06:23,833 --> 00:06:26,000
- you're having an affair...
- Enrico, you're wrong.

116
00:06:26,133 --> 00:06:27,767
- You're wrong.
- What's wrong about it?

117
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:28,867
Enough!

118
00:06:30,167 --> 00:06:32,000
Tyrone, you're fired.

119
00:06:33,033 --> 00:06:34,867
And I'll make sure...

120
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,800
that no one hires you
for any job...

121
00:06:36,933 --> 00:06:38,300
anywhere in Solmera City.

122
00:06:41,267 --> 00:06:42,767
And you, Serina...

123
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:45,433
you'll never set foot again
in my home.

124
00:06:45,567 --> 00:06:47,167
No, no...

125
00:06:47,300 --> 00:06:49,500
And from now on, my lawyer will
be the one speaking to you

126
00:06:49,633 --> 00:06:50,667
regarding our annulment.

127
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,667
What? What annulment?

128
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,833
What annulment? Enrico, please!

129
00:06:54,967 --> 00:06:57,167
Please, Enrico!

130
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,667
Enrico!

131
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:05,967
Idiot! This is all your fault.

132
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,933
You're such an idiot!
We got caught because of you!

133
00:07:08,067 --> 00:07:09,767
What was I supposed to do?
We already got caught.

134
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:11,733
No, this can't happen.

135
00:07:11,867 --> 00:07:14,600
I can't just lose everything
I've worked so hard for.

136
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:16,400
I can't become poor again.

137
00:07:18,667 --> 00:07:19,933
What are you going to do?

138
00:07:25,433 --> 00:07:26,833
You said...

139
00:07:26,967 --> 00:07:30,533
You said there was someone
who could take care of Enrico?

140
00:07:30,667 --> 00:07:31,733
Right?

141
00:07:31,867 --> 00:07:41,100
[FOREBODING MUSIC]

142
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:46,567
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC]

143
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:49,267
I wish you had never
disappeared, Isabella.

144
00:07:50,333 --> 00:07:53,233
I wish I had never opened
my heart again.

145
00:07:56,367 --> 00:07:58,767
I wish I had never fallen
in love with Serina.

146
00:08:02,133 --> 00:08:03,600
Now that we're no longer
together...

147
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:11,633
I'll focus on finding
our princess.

148
00:08:11,767 --> 00:08:16,167
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

149
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:19,733
As long as I'm alive...

150
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,233
I'll never stop searching
for you, my child.

151
00:08:34,667 --> 00:08:36,033
I won't give up.

152
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,933
Even if so many people say that
you're already dead.

153
00:08:50,933 --> 00:08:54,067
[TIME BOMB TICKING]

154
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,767
[EXPLOSION]

155
00:08:55,933 --> 00:08:57,967
[GRIPPING MUSIC]

156
00:09:02,933 --> 00:09:04,900
So, Doc, what did you find?

157
00:09:05,033 --> 00:09:07,867
Why did my son collapse
the other day?

158
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:12,300
Neil, I found lesions
on your son's vocal cords.

159
00:09:12,433 --> 00:09:15,900
This is commonly seen in singers
who are severely overworked.

160
00:09:17,133 --> 00:09:19,200
<i>I think what Miguel needs
right now</i>

161
00:09:19,333 --> 00:09:21,267
<i>is at least six months of rest.</i>

162
00:09:22,933 --> 00:09:25,833
Otherwise, his singing voice
could suffer permanent damage.

163
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,867
Six months?

164
00:09:29,733 --> 00:09:31,567
Doc, six months isn't possible.

165
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:33,767
My son has too many commitments.

166
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,767
Siklab has a world tour.

167
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:39,533
Surely we can manage this
with medication,

168
00:09:39,667 --> 00:09:40,767
treatment, therapy,
or something.

169
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:44,567
Dad, didn't you hear
what the doctor said?

170
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:45,933
I need to rest.

171
00:09:46,767 --> 00:09:48,200
I'm sure my fans
will understand.

172
00:09:49,267 --> 00:09:51,133
No, they won't.

173
00:09:52,533 --> 00:09:54,400
You know, Miguel,

174
00:09:54,533 --> 00:09:55,933
you're partly to blame
for this too.

175
00:09:56,867 --> 00:10:00,400
Instead of resting,
you keep busking.

176
00:10:01,933 --> 00:10:03,967
And now, you'll be gone
for six months.

177
00:10:05,267 --> 00:10:08,733
Do you know how long six months
is in this industry?

178
00:10:08,867 --> 00:10:10,533
People will forget you.

179
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:15,167
Siklab is at its peak right now
and you're going to step away?

180
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:17,533
What are you thinking?

181
00:10:19,767 --> 00:10:21,733
[CELLPHONE RINGS]

182
00:10:23,567 --> 00:10:24,467
Hello, Randel.

183
00:10:26,133 --> 00:10:29,533
Contact our international
tour teams.

184
00:10:29,667 --> 00:10:32,200
- I just need some air.
- If Miguel has to lip-sync

185
00:10:32,333 --> 00:10:33,433
- so this tour can continue...
- I'm going to do some busking.

186
00:10:33,567 --> 00:10:34,733
- then that's what we'll do.
- Take me there.

187
00:10:34,900 --> 00:10:36,100
As long as this tour goes ahead.

188
00:10:38,433 --> 00:10:39,267
Yes.

189
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:41,200
Miguel...

190
00:10:42,167 --> 00:10:43,167
Miguel, where are...

191
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,100
Miguel!

192
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,200
Oh, Zion.

193
00:10:56,500 --> 00:11:01,000
["FIRST LOVE" INSTRUMENTAL]

194
00:11:01,133 --> 00:11:02,133
It's beautiful.

195
00:11:05,167 --> 00:11:06,633
Your crown looks beautiful.

196
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:07,733
It suits you perfectly.

197
00:11:09,667 --> 00:11:12,533
Good thing the online seller
responded quickly.

198
00:11:12,667 --> 00:11:14,767
At least we got it, right?

199
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:15,700
Let me see.

200
00:11:17,633 --> 00:11:18,500
Thank you.

201
00:11:20,033 --> 00:11:21,767
Shall we start?

202
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:23,133
Sure, let's do it.

203
00:11:23,267 --> 00:11:24,000
Okay.

204
00:11:26,133 --> 00:11:28,433
Glasses don't really work
for a prince.

205
00:11:28,567 --> 00:11:29,800
Here, sit down.

206
00:11:29,933 --> 00:11:31,533
Right here.

207
00:11:31,667 --> 00:11:32,800
There.

208
00:11:34,700 --> 00:11:36,533
Angel, I can't see
without those.

209
00:11:37,767 --> 00:11:39,600
You won't need them anymore.

210
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:42,333
What's that?

211
00:11:42,467 --> 00:11:44,667
Remember when I asked you

212
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,900
about your prescription
the other night?

213
00:11:47,033 --> 00:11:48,933
I bought it for you.

214
00:11:49,067 --> 00:11:50,600
For me?

215
00:11:50,733 --> 00:11:52,067
Yes.

216
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,100
It's my way of repaying you

217
00:11:53,233 --> 00:11:55,633
for everything you've done
for me.

218
00:11:55,767 --> 00:11:58,233
You know, at my old school,

219
00:11:58,367 --> 00:12:00,667
I didn't really have
many friends because...

220
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:01,700
they said I was a nerd.

221
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:05,167
You're the first person
I've ever become this close to.

222
00:12:06,833 --> 00:12:07,667
Look up.

223
00:12:11,033 --> 00:12:12,000
There.

224
00:12:16,367 --> 00:12:17,933
Oh, see?

225
00:12:18,067 --> 00:12:19,400
They suit you much better.

226
00:12:19,533 --> 00:12:20,700
You look cuter.

227
00:12:20,833 --> 00:12:21,700
Cuter?

228
00:12:23,167 --> 00:12:26,633
Cute enough for Charm
to notice you.

229
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:30,667
Weren't you planning to ask her
to the Siklab concert?

230
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:32,667
After all, you still
have the tickets.

231
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,667
Mr. Moon never claimed them
anyway.

232
00:12:38,067 --> 00:12:39,200
Oh, right.

233
00:12:39,333 --> 00:12:40,867
I really hope she says yes,
Angel.

234
00:12:42,067 --> 00:12:43,300
She'll definitely say yes.

235
00:12:46,467 --> 00:12:47,433
Thank you so much.

236
00:12:52,633 --> 00:12:53,333
Here you go!

237
00:12:53,467 --> 00:12:55,533
- Matcha for energy!
- Of course.

238
00:12:55,667 --> 00:12:57,133
So, how's it going?

239
00:12:57,267 --> 00:13:00,700
Well, I hacked
into the campus CCTV,

240
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:02,733
and I got the footage

241
00:13:02,867 --> 00:13:05,667
from when we were playing
the lie detector game.

242
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:07,333
Oh, my gosh. Let me see.

243
00:13:07,467 --> 00:13:08,633
- Now using AI...
- Yeah.

244
00:13:08,767 --> 00:13:11,967
I edited it to make it look like
Calix is admitting

245
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:13,467
that he likes Angel.

246
00:13:14,767 --> 00:13:16,133
- Want to see it?
- Show me.

247
00:13:16,267 --> 00:13:16,967
[ADIE CHUCKLES]

248
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,733
<i>Do you have feelings for Angel?</i>

249
00:13:24,433 --> 00:13:26,400
<i>What kind of stupid
question is that, Charm?</i>

250
00:13:26,533 --> 00:13:27,800
<i> Of course I do.</i>

251
00:13:27,933 --> 00:13:30,367
[BOTH LAUGH]

252
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:32,000
- Oh, my gosh.
- See that?

253
00:13:32,133 --> 00:13:34,467
See? It even has subtitles.

254
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,000
Now, the next step is,

255
00:13:36,133 --> 00:13:38,633
I'll post this in our group chat
for Section Narra

256
